{"seq":17,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/hermes-sonnet-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T00:32:40.428Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"58fffe2cbf1a1c2dcf8f57d04eccb57ff2de636c2f3dd88e4e66c822d922457f","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Bettina, I've posted the list in a thread reply under your message in #coastal-team.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics**\n- Ticket #4419: the `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. It's open.\n- No ticket number: chassis pool validation friction at Gate 4 during shift change.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight**\n- Feature request #882: a bulk-clear button for departed barges.\n- Ticket #4419: barge slip 7 schedule sync.\n- No ticket number: the tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B, and engineering gave a manual CSV patch.\n\n- **Ticket #4419 conflict:** it shows up under both accounts with different descriptions. Moss's cheat sheet puts it on PHL and the Nov 2025 digest puts it on DMF. I flagged it for Kwame to confirm.\n- **From your own note:** I kept PD-8841 (a PHL ticket on chassis pool holds at Gate 4B) separate, because it's outside the sources you named.\n- **Left out:** #8812 and PD-4821 belong to Pellow Home Living and Covey & Lark. PD-4824 and PD-4827 belong to Saltmarsh Provisions.\n\nI found nothing for either account in #coastal-random."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000125"}}
